-- 2026-10-13 — EmmaDataKing (emmadataking.com) as an MTN supplier. Applied via execute_sql.
-- suppliers: code emmadataking, display_order 15, metadata.topup_fee_rate 0.03 (they charge 3% on top-ups).
-- supplier_product_mappings (inactive until MTN is switched to them in Admin → Suppliers):
--   MTN 1..30GB → list YELLO (normal queue), supplier_price = their price; 40/50GB → EXPRESS_YELLO (165/200).
-- Trigger orders_dbh_mtn_approval widened: any supplier's "not approved / unapproved / pending approval" refusal
--   on a paid MTN order becomes the awaiting_verification hold (was DBH's exact wording only).
-- cron job 14 'sync-emmadataking-order-status' every minute (resend loop + /order-status poll).
-- Secret: EMMADATAKING_API_KEY (X-API-Key). Their webhook (HMAC with whsec_…) not wired yet; polling covers delivery.
-- verify-mtn-numbers now re-sends approved numbers through MTN's current preferred supplier, not always DBH.
-- Observed: their /verify-number is a live MTN line check (numbers DBH holds as unapproved came back verified).
-- Owner: no EXPRESS_YELLO at all. The 40/50GB EXPRESS rows are switched off with metadata.disabled, and
-- admin_set_network_supplier no longer re-activates rows carrying metadata.disabled (and counts/missing use active
-- rows only). With MTN on EmmaDataKing, 40GB and 50GB have no active mapping and would be held for review.

-- Fallback supplier per network (applied via execute_sql):
--   alter table phase1.networks add column fallback_supplier_id uuid references phase1.suppliers(id);
--   phase1.admin_set_network_fallback(p_actor, p_network_code, p_supplier_code|null): must differ from the main supplier;
--   activates the fallback's non-disabled mappings for that network.
-- Behaviour (_shared/fallback.ts): an order gets the fallback ONCE (marker event supplier.fallback).
--   at purchase: main supplier refuses / does not know the bundle → sent to fallback immediately (fulfillment.ts);
--   after acceptance: main supplier reports refunded/failed (DBH silent MTN refund incl.) → order reset and queued
--   for the fallback's resend loop (sync-dbh-order-status / sync-emmadataking-order-status, which now resend by their own supplier id).
-- verify-mtn-numbers re-sends DBH-approved numbers through DBH again (the approval is on DBH's channel).

-- Finance: EmmaDataKing float account (was missing, so Record top-up could not be saved against it):
--   insert into phase1.finance_accounts (code,name,kind,supplier_id,sort_order)
--   values ('float_emmadataking','Supplier float · EmmaDataKing','asset',<emmadataking id>,23);
-- First top-up recorded via finance_record_topup('emmadataking', 200, 2026-10-13 20:21Z, 'bank') → fee 6 (3%).
-- Fallback is once per ATTEMPT: supplier.fallback events are counted only since the latest admin.retry event,
-- so a manual Retry (both suppliers were empty, main still is) can still hand the order to the fallback.
-- 13 Oct late: a purchase that gets NO answer (HTTP 0/408/5xx) is ambiguous, not a refusal. fulfillment.ts now asks the
-- supplier by our reference (adapter.findByReference, EmmaDataKing only so far): held → keep it there
-- (event supplier.recovered_after_timeout); refunded/unknown → failure, fallback allowed; lookup impossible or no
-- lookup (DBH) → failure a person must check, NO fallback. Cause: YG-C3680ED132 was delivered by both EDK and DBH.
-- Loophole sweep (13 Oct night), all in _shared/fulfillment.ts:
--   * a thrown purchase (connection refused, DNS, our timeout) is an ambiguous outcome (http 0), logged, never a refusal;
--   * before re-sending to a supplier already tried for the order, ask it by our reference (findByReference) and adopt
--     the order if it is held (event supplier.already_held);
--   * the idempotency key is reused when the last attempt at that supplier got no answer (admin Retry no longer clears it);
--   * ambiguous + no lookup possible → order stays processing with supplier_retry_after +3 min (event supplier.no_answer),
--     re-checked by that supplier's resend loop up to 3 times, then failed_needs_review.
--   sync-instantdata-order-status gained the same resend loop as the DBH/EmmaDataKing syncs.
-- Fallback moves an order ONLY on a confirmed refund (EmmaDataKing REFUNDED, DBH refunded/refund), never on FAILED/REJECTED:
-- "failed" is not "money back" and the supplier could still re-run it. FAILED orders wait in Needs review with a
-- "NOT refunded yet; confirm with the supplier" reason. (Fallback is switched OFF by the owner for now.)
-- 14 Oct: EmmaDataKing gets a distinct reference per attempt (edkRef: YG-x, YG-x-R1, YG-x-R2…; PurchaseContext.attempt =
-- number of earlier purchase logs at that supplier) so lookups are never ambiguous; the pre-send lookup checks every
-- earlier attempt. sync-emmadataking-order-status "refund watch": Needs-review orders marked "NOT refunded yet" are polled;
-- on REFUNDED they go to the network's fallback (if set) or are re-labelled "safe to Retry".
-- 14 Oct 05:30: a supplier FAILED/REJECTED that is NOT yet refunded keeps the order IN PROGRESS (status processing,
-- supplier_status FAILED, event supplier.failed_awaiting_refund) — Needs review is only for orders a person can act on.
-- Once REFUNDED: fallback if set, else failed_needs_review "safe to Retry". EDK adapter stores a purchase id only when
-- the purchase was accepted. AG-77329A765C and YG-33C0F1DFA6 moved to processing/FAILED by hand.
-- 14 Oct 09:10: phase1.admin_supplier_last_deliveries(p_actor) — per supplier, the latest delivered order (last 7 days):
-- order, bundle, network, sent_at (that supplier's fulfillment_started event, else paid_at), delivered_at, minutes.
-- Shown on Admin → Suppliers cards ("Last delivery: N min · MTN 2GB · time"), green ≤30, amber ≤90, red beyond.
-- 14 Oct 09:40 — per-bundle pinned supplier ("Always via", Admin → Suppliers → network → bundle):
--   alter table phase1.data_products add column forced_supplier_id uuid references phase1.suppliers(id);
--   phase1.admin_set_product_supplier(p_actor, p_product_id, p_supplier_code|null) — admin only; supplier must be active
--   and sell the bundle (non-disabled mapping, activated). MTN 5, 6, 40, 50GB pinned to DataBundlesHub.
-- fulfillment.ts routes: opts.supplierId → product.forced_supplier_id → network.preferred_supplier_id.
-- fallback.ts: a pinned bundle falls back to the network fallback, or to the network main when the pin IS the fallback
--   (still only after a confirmed refund). sync-dbh: MTN verification (silent) refunds never leave DBH any more.
--   + data_products.forced_fallback_supplier_id and phase1.admin_set_product_fallback(p_actor, p_product_id, p_supplier_code|null):
--     a pinned bundle has its OWN fallback (must differ from Always via; null = no fallback). Set: 5GB/6GB → EmmaDataKing, 40/50GB none.
--   fallback.ts: pinned bundle → its own fallback only; unpinned → the network's fallback.
-- 14 Oct 11:00: delivery_speed() / delivery_speed_by_network() count only orders a supplier is really working on
--   (delivered, or open with a live supplier reference and no failed/refunded/not_approved status); the clock starts at the
--   CURRENT supplier's fulfillment_started event (restarts after a fallback), else paid_at.
-- admin-order-action "try_supplier" {supplierCode}: admin sends a REFUNDED (or never-sent) paid order to a chosen active
--   supplier that sells the bundle; refused while the current supplier may still hold it. Writes a supplier.fallback event
--   (stage admin_try_supplier) and sends via fulfillOrder({supplierId, viaFallback:true}). Orders page: "Try another supplier" dropdown.
-- 14 Oct 11:30: on a CLEAR refusal (e.g. insufficient balance) fulfillment.ts asks the supplier by reference before
--   any fallback; if they hold it queued the order stays (event supplier.recovered_after_timeout). Lookup failure → no fallback.
-- Admin badge: E→D tooltip carries the fallback reason; a ₵ mark means the first supplier had no float.
